1. Definitions

“Software” means the Euryphos source code, object code, and accompanying documentation in this repository, but only to the extent the Licensor has authority to license that material.

“Individual” means a natural person acting on their own behalf and not on behalf of an Organization.

“Personal Use” means use solely by an Individual for that Individual’s personal devices, household, home lab, hobby, or self-directed learning. Personal Use must not be performed for, on behalf of, or as part of the operations of an Organization, and must not provide a service to customers or generate a commercial benefit for an Organization.

“Organization” means a company, corporation, partnership, business, government body, nonprofit, school, university, agency, or other legal or organized entity.

“Commercial or Organizational Use” means any use of the Software by or for an Organization, including use to manage or monitor organizational devices or infrastructure; internal business, public-sector, nonprofit, or institutional operations; provision of services to customers; consulting or managed services; or use connected with revenue-generating activity. Whether the use itself generates revenue is not determinative.

“Licensor” means the copyright holder(s) or other rights holder(s) authorized to grant the applicable rights.

2. Free Personal Use Grant

Subject to this license, the Licensor grants an Individual a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free, non-transferable license to download, reproduce, compile, execute, and modify the Software solely for Personal Use.

No fee is charged for the Personal Use rights granted in this section.

3. Commercial and Organizational License Required

The Personal Use grant does not authorize Commercial or Organizational Use.

Before any Commercial or Organizational Use, the user must obtain a separate written commercial license from the applicable rights holder. This requirement applies even when an Individual downloads or operates the Software on behalf of an Organization, and even when the deployment is internal, nonprofit, educational, government, evaluation-only, or not directly revenue-generating.

No commercial rights are granted by access to this repository, by possession of a copy, or by this Personal Use license.

